# compliance_exceptions.conf - approved compliance exceptions, shared by rds-patch-compliance,
# rds-backup-compliance and rds-compliance-report (same file and format in all three).
#
# Copy to compliance_exceptions.conf next to the script (picked up automatically), or pass --exceptions FILE.
# No file = no exceptions (reports exactly as before).
#
# One entry per line, all five fields required:
#   account_id | identifier | scope | expires | reason
#     account_id  12-digit AWS account
#     identifier  DB instance or cluster identifier (exact, case-insensitive; no wildcards; any region)
#     scope       patch, backup or patch,backup
#     expires     YYYY-MM-DD (UTC), mandatory; the last day the exception applies
#     reason      free text (ticket, owner, why); may contain |
# A bad line (missing field, bad account / scope / date, duplicate account + identifier for the same scope)
# stops the run with file:line. # comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Matched and not expired: shown as "Compliant (exception)" and counted as compliant in every %;
#   the real status is kept (actual_status). Flags: "expiring soon" (14 days or less), "no longer needed"
#   (the server is already compliant). Expired: evaluated normally and flagged "exception expired".
# Applied when the report is built; --save-data files never change.

111111111111 | legacy-aurora-pg12 | patch        | 2026-12-31 | Decommission in December, CHG-1234 (owner: dba-team)
111111111111 | reports-pg         | patch,backup | 2027-03-31 | Vendor-pinned version, backups by vendor tool | INC-77
222222222222 | dev-docdb          | backup       | 2027-01-31 | Dev cluster, data rebuilt from source
